-- title:
--   Deck group of order dividing (ℓ-1)/2 for q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $\iota_0 : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota_0(\zeta)=\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $H_1\le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb{Q}$ of the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$. Finally let $G\le K\simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[L]} K$ be the subgroup generated by those $\tau$ for which some $\gamma\in\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ lies in $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and satisfies `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`, i.e. for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, $p_g\neq 0$, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $p_f/p_g$, and every $\iota : L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta)=\exp(2\pi i/q)$, one has $\iota(\tau x)\cdot (g\mid_k \gamma^{-1}_{(q)})^{\wedge} = (f\mid_k \gamma^{-1}_{(q)})^{\wedge}$ as $q$-expansions, where $\gamma^{-1}_{(q)}$ denotes the conjugate $\begin{pmatrix} a & b/q\\ qc & d\end{pmatrix}$ of $\gamma^{-1}=\begin{pmatrix}a&b\\c&d\end{pmatrix}$. Then $G$ is finite and $\#G$ divides $(\ell-1)/2$ (natural-number division).
--
--   This bounds the group of deck transformations generated by the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ on the base-changed function field of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$: the diamond operators in question are indexed by $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$ modulo $\pm 1$, whence the bound $(\ell-1)/2$ rather than $\ell-1$. The sharper form at $q=2$ is what the auxiliary-level results on invariants and formal smoothness of the rigid chart require, since there the order of the group must be invertible in residue characteristic $2$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevelOne_finite_and_natCard_dvd_div_two_of_eq_closure_isLevelAutAt_gamma_of_eq_two_of_dvd.lean

